    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# 🧩 Exercise: Calculate BMI & Classify Health Risk\n\n## 🎯 Objective\nIn this exercise, you will:\n- Learn how to process structured data in n8n\n- Calculate **BMI (Body Mass Index)** using JavaScript in a Code node\n- Classify users into **BMI categories**\n- Practice using Code, IF, and Filter nodes\n\n---\n\n## 📥 Input Data\nYou are given a list of users with the following fields:\n\n- `user_id`\n- `age`\n- `height` (cm)\n- `weight` (kg)\n- `salary`\n- `premium` (may contain `null`)\n\nEach item represents **one user**.\n\n---\n\n## 🧮 Step 1: BMI Calculation\n\n### BMI Formula\n",
        "height": 800,
        "width": 848
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -320,
        992
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "b751ea63-aff0-4248-a9fb-309d65340332",
      "name": "Sticky Note3"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "\n### Important Notes\n- Height must be converted from **centimeters (cm)** to **meters (m)**\n- Round the BMI value to **2 decimal places**\n- If height or weight is missing, BMI should be set to `null`\n\n---\n\n## 🏷️ Step 2: BMI Category Classification\n\nAfter calculating BMI, classify each user into one of the following categories:\n\n| BMI Range            | Category        | Description                  |\n|----------------------|-----------------|------------------------------|\n| BMI < 18.5           | Underweight     | Lower than normal body weight|\n| 18.5 ≤ BMI < 25      | Normal          | Healthy weight range         |\n| 25 ≤ BMI < 30        | Overweight      | Higher than normal weight    |\n| BMI ≥ 30             | Obese           | High health risk             |\n\n---\n\n## 🔀 Suggested Workflow\n1. **Code Node**\n   - Calculate BMI\n   - Add `bmi` field to each user\n\n2. **Code Node / IF Node**\n   - Determine `bmi_category` based on BMI value\n\n3. **Filter / IF Node (Optional)**\n   - Find users with:\n     - BMI ≥ 25\n     - Missing `premium`\n     - High health risk\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 Learning Outcome\nBy completing this exercise, you should be able to:\n- Understand how n8n processes data item by item\n- Apply mathematical formulas in automation workflows\n- Handle `null` values safely\n- Turn raw data into **actionable insights**\n\n🚀 Bonus Challenge:\n- Calculate average BMI per group\n- Recommend insurance premium based on BMI category\n",
        "height": 1008,
        "width": 976
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        544,
        992
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "6d9125c7-3aaa-4c1e-9b65-f93f8960f870",
      "name": "Sticky Note6"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "/**\n * This Code node calculates BMI (Body Mass Index)\n * BMI formula:\n *   BMI = weight (kg) / (height (m))^2\n *\n * Assumptions:\n * - height is provided in centimeters (cm)\n * - weight is provided in kilograms (kg)\n */\n\nreturn items.map((item) => {\n  // Extract data from the current item\n  const heightCm = item.json.height;\n  const weightKg = item.json.weight;\n\n  let bmi = null;\n\n  // Validate input values\n  if (heightCm && weightKg) {\n    // Convert height from centimeters to meters\n    const heightMeter = heightCm / 100;\n\n    // Calculate BMI\n    bmi = weightKg / (heightMeter * heightMeter);\n\n    // Round BMI to 2 decimal places\n    bmi = Number(bmi.toFixed(2));\n  }\n\n  // Add BMI back to the original JSON\n  return {\n    json: {\n      ...item.json,\n      bmi,\n    },\n  };\n});\n"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1136,
        304
      ],
      "id": "f58b3009-32e8-4381-a96e-063559636312",
      "name": "BMI Calculator"
    },
